THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
--------------------

Nothing is downloaded from a third party at run time.

This action downloads and executes exactly one binary, ours, verified against a
digest pinned in pins.env before it runs. It fetches nothing else, from anyone.
That is a deliberate difference from the Visiblaze SAST action, which downloads
Opengrep and therefore also downloads cosign to verify Opengrep's signature.

The scanner does, however, EMBED a rule pack that includes detection rules
derived from Trivy:

Trivy - https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy
    Copyright Aqua Security Software Ltd.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    Visiblaze's secret rule pack carries detection patterns adapted from Trivy's
    built-in secret rules (pkg/fanal/secret/builtin-rules.go, v0.70.0). Rule
    identifiers are kept identical to Trivy's on purpose, so that a repository
    scanned by both engines reports one finding rather than two. No Trivy code is
    linked, bundled or executed by this action.

    A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is in LICENSE, which is the same
    licence this repository is under.

That is a deliberate difference from the Visiblaze SAST action, which downloads
Opengrep and therefore also downloads cosign to verify Opengrep's signature.
Credential detection is regular expressions over text, so implementing it in our
own scanner leaves one artefact to trust instead of three — and no upstream
project whose release process could change under us.
